    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ae2Q2eliPwvw"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "# Part A: Build Your Own Neural Network (CS231n style)\n",
        "\n",
        "The network:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "input (784 pixels) → [W1, b1] → ReLU hidden layer (256 units, dropout) → [W2, b2] → softmax (10 classes)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4. Initialise the parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "| Parameter | Shape | Role |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| `W1` | 784 × 256 | weights from pixels to hidden units |\n",
        "| `b1` | 256 | hidden-unit biases |\n",
        "| `W2` | 256 × 10 | weights from hidden units to classes |\n",
        "| `b2` | 10 | class biases |\n",
        "\n",
        "Biases start at zero. Weights start as small random numbers using **He initialisation** (standard deviation √(2 / inputs)), which keeps signals at a healthy size as they pass through ReLU layers. `add_bias()` adds a bias vector to every row of a matrix."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7yEJiCBZPwvw"
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "init_net <- function(D, H, K) {\n",
        "  list(W1 = matrix(rnorm(D * H, sd = sqrt(2 / D)), D, H), b1 = rep(0, H),\n",
        "       W2 = matrix(rnorm(H * K, sd = sqrt(2 / H)), H, K), b2 = rep(0, K))\n",
        "}\n",
        "add_bias <- function(M, b) M + matrix(b, nrow(M), length(b), byrow = TRUE)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5_ZjRJRdPwvw"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Forward pass, loss and backpropagation\n",
        "\n",
        "**Forward pass**\n",
        "1. Hidden layer: `h = ReLU(X · W1 + b1)`. ReLU zeroes negative values, which lets the network learn non-linear patterns.\n",
        "2. **Dropout** (training only): randomly switch off 20% of hidden units on each step, scaling up the rest to compensate. This stops the network relying too heavily on any single unit, so it generalises better.\n",
        "3. Scores: `h · W2 + b2`, then **softmax** turns the scores into probabilities. We subtract each row's maximum first so `exp()` can't overflow.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Loss:** **cross-entropy**, the average of `-log(probability of the correct class)`, plus an **L2 penalty** on the weights to discourage overfitting.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Backward pass:** the chain rule carries the error back through each layer to give the gradient of every parameter. The softmax and cross-entropy gradient is simply `probabilities − 1` at the correct class. ReLU and dropout pass gradient only through the units that were active."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RIi2ccYZPwvw"
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "loss_grad <- function(net, X, y, reg, drop = 0) {\n",
        "  N <- nrow(X)\n",
        "\n",
        "  # ---- forward ----\n",
        "  h <- pmax(add_bias(X %*% net$W1, net$b1), 0)\n",
        "  if (drop > 0) {\n",
        "    mask <- (matrix(runif(length(h)), nrow(h)) > drop) / (1 - drop)\n",
        "    h <- h * mask\n",
        "  }\n",
        "  scores <- add_bias(h %*% net$W2, net$b2)\n",
        "  scores <- scores - scores[cbind(1:N, max.col(scores))]\n",
        "  p <- exp(scores); p <- p / rowSums(p)\n",
        "\n",
        "  loss <- -mean(log(p[cbind(1:N, y + 1)])) +\n",
        "          0.5 * reg * (sum(net$W1^2) + sum(net$W2^2))\n",
        "\n",
        "  # ---- backward ----\n",
        "  dscores <- p\n",
        "  dscores[cbind(1:N, y + 1)] <- dscores[cbind(1:N, y + 1)] - 1\n",
        "  dscores <- dscores / N\n",
        "  dW2 <- t(h) %*% dscores + reg * net$W2\n",
        "  db2 <- colSums(dscores)\n",
        "  dh  <- dscores %*% t(net$W2)\n",
        "  dh[h <= 0] <- 0                     # ReLU (and dropped units) pass no gradient\n",
        "  if (drop > 0) dh <- dh * mask       # dropout scaling\n",
        "  dW1 <- t(X) %*% dh + reg * net$W1\n",
        "  db1 <- colSums(dh)\n",
        "\n",
        "  list(loss = loss, grads = list(W1 = dW1, b1 = db1, W2 = dW2, b2 = db2))\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "predict_net <- function(net, X) {    # no dropout at prediction time\n",
        "  h <- pmax(add_bias(X %*% net$W1, net$b1), 0)\n",
        "  max.col(add_bias(h %*% net$W2, net$b2)) - 1\n",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k3w5i-kRPwvx"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Sanity check:** with random weights the network should spread its guesses evenly across the 10 classes, so the starting loss should be about **−log(1/10) ≈ 2.30**."
      ]
