    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jtmXwdiOPwvx"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 6. The Adam optimiser\n",
        "\n",
        "Plain gradient descent uses one step size for every weight. **Adam** adapts the step size per weight:\n",
        "\n",
        "- It keeps a running average of each gradient (**momentum**, `m`), which smooths out noisy updates.\n",
        "- It keeps a running average of each squared gradient (`v`), which shrinks steps for weights whose gradients are large or erratic.\n",
        "- It applies **bias correction**, because both averages start at zero.\n",
        "\n",
        "It usually trains faster and reaches better results than plain gradient descent, and it's still only a few lines of R."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GTyASDFzPwvx"
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "adam_init <- function(net) list(m = lapply(net, `*`, 0), v = lapply(net, `*`, 0), t = 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "adam_step <- function(net, grads, st, lr, b1 = 0.9, b2 = 0.999, eps = 1e-8) {\n",
        "  st$t <- st$t + 1\n",
        "  for (nm in names(net)) {\n",
        "    st$m[[nm]] <- b1 * st$m[[nm]] + (1 - b1) * grads[[nm]]\n",
        "    st$v[[nm]] <- b2 * st$v[[nm]] + (1 - b2) * grads[[nm]]^2\n",
        "    m_hat <- st$m[[nm]] / (1 - b1^st$t)\n",
        "    v_hat <- st$v[[nm]] / (1 - b2^st$t)\n",
        "    net[[nm]] <- net[[nm]] - lr * m_hat / (sqrt(v_hat) + eps)\n",
        "  }\n",
        "  list(net = net, st = st)\n",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "IhbKFPFVPwvx"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Train the hand-built network\n",
        "\n",
        "Each **epoch** shuffles the training set, splits it into minibatches of 128, and takes one Adam step per batch. The learning rate decays by 10% each epoch so the steps get finer as training settles. This takes several minutes because base R is doing all the maths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "R0tHV519Pwvx",
        "outputId": "30c13548-b3ac-4857-e249-ab56803f9fd7"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "epoch  1  train acc 0.9462  val acc 0.9374\n",
            "epoch  2  train acc 0.9700  val acc 0.9555\n",
            "epoch  3  train acc 0.9756  val acc 0.9619\n",
            "epoch  4  train acc 0.9810  val acc 0.9655\n",
            "epoch  5  train acc 0.9830  val acc 0.9657\n",
            "epoch  6  train acc 0.9878  val acc 0.9683\n",
            "epoch  7  train acc 0.9884  val acc 0.9688\n",
            "epoch  8  train acc 0.9892  val acc 0.9698\n",
            "epoch  9  train acc 0.9926  val acc 0.9712\n",
            "epoch 10  train acc 0.9932  val acc 0.9698\n",
            "epoch 11  train acc 0.9938  val acc 0.9714\n",
            "epoch 12  train acc 0.9940  val acc 0.9710\n",
            "epoch 13  train acc 0.9950  val acc 0.9712\n",
            "epoch 14  train acc 0.9954  val acc 0.9731\n",
            "epoch 15  train acc 0.9960  val acc 0.9721\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "set.seed(42)\n",
        "net <- init_net(784, 256, 10); st <- adam_init(net)\n",
        "lr <- 1e-3; reg <- 1e-4; drop <- 0.2; batch <- 128; epochs <- 15\n",
        "hist_a <- data.frame(epoch = integer(), train_acc = numeric(), val_acc = numeric())\n",
        "sub <- sample(nrow(Xtr), 5000)   # subset for a quick training-accuracy check\n",
        "\n",
        "for (ep in 1:epochs) {\n",
        "  perm <- sample(nrow(Xtr))\n",
        "  for (s in seq(1, nrow(Xtr), by = batch)) {\n",
        "    b   <- perm[s:min(s + batch - 1, nrow(Xtr))]\n",
        "    out <- loss_grad(net, Xtr[b, , drop = FALSE], ytr[b], reg, drop)\n",
        "    upd <- adam_step(net, out$grads, st, lr); net <- upd$net; st <- upd$st\n",
        "  }\n",
        "  lr <- lr * 0.9\n",
        "  tr  <- mean(predict_net(net, Xtr[sub, ]) == ytr[sub])\n",
        "  val <- mean(predict_net(net, Xval) == yval)\n",
        "  hist_a[ep, ] <- c(ep, tr, val)\n",
        "  cat(sprintf(\"epoch %2d  train acc %.4f  val acc %.4f\\n\", ep, tr, val))\n",
        "}\n",
        "scratch_val_acc <- val"
      ]
    },
