      "source": [
        "## 11. Training and prediction functions\n",
        "\n",
        "**Training** uses the **Adam** optimiser (the same algorithm we wrote by hand in Part A, now built in) with a **one-cycle learning-rate schedule**. The learning rate warms up, peaks, then smoothly decays to almost zero by the last batch. This reliably gives fast training and a well-settled final model.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Prediction** switches the model to evaluation mode (dropout off, BN uses its learned statistics), turns off gradient tracking to save memory, and returns the softmax **probabilities** for each class. We keep probabilities rather than just the top class so we can average several models later.\n",
        "\n",
        "The settings adapt to your hardware: more epochs and more ensemble members on a GPU."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "o0ShtvPCPwvy"
      },
      "execution_count": 15,
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "EPOCHS   <- if (on_gpu) 20 else 8\n",
        "N_MODELS <- if (on_gpu) 5  else 1\n",
        "BATCH    <- 128\n",
        "\n",
        "predict_probs <- function(model, x) {\n",
        "  model$eval()\n",
        "  out <- list()\n",
        "  with_no_grad({\n",
        "    for (s in seq(1, x$size(1), by = 1000)) {\n",
        "      e <- min(s + 999, x$size(1))\n",
        "      out[[length(out) + 1]] <- as_array(nnf_softmax(model(x[s:e, .., drop = FALSE]), dim = 2)$cpu())\n",
        "    }\n",
        "  })\n",
        "  do.call(rbind, out)\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "train_cnn <- function(x, y, epochs = EPOCHS, seed = 1, x_val = NULL, y_val = NULL) {\n",
        "  set.seed(seed); torch_manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "  model <- cnn()$to(device = dev)\n",
        "  opt   <- optim_adam(model$parameters, lr = 1e-3)\n",
        "  n     <- x$size(1)\n",
        "  sched <- lr_one_cycle(opt, max_lr = 3e-3, total_steps = epochs * ceiling(n / BATCH) + 1)\n",
        "  hist  <- data.frame(epoch = integer(), loss = numeric(), val_acc = numeric())\n",
        "\n",
        "  for (ep in 1:epochs) {\n",
        "    model$train()\n",
        "    perm <- sample(n); total <- 0\n",
        "    for (s in seq(1, n, by = BATCH)) {\n",
        "      b  <- perm[s:min(s + BATCH - 1, n)]\n",
        "      xb <- augment(x[b, .., drop = FALSE])\n",
        "      opt$zero_grad()\n",
        "      loss <- nnf_cross_entropy(model(xb), y[b])\n",
        "      loss$backward()\n",
        "      opt$step(); sched$step()\n",
        "      total <- total + loss$item() * length(b)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    val_acc <- if (!is.null(x_val)) mean(max.col(predict_probs(model, x_val)) - 1 == y_val) else NA\n",
        "    hist[ep, ] <- c(ep, total / n, val_acc)\n",
        "    cat(sprintf(\"  epoch %2d  loss %.4f%s\\n\", ep, total / n,\n",
        "                if (is.na(val_acc)) \"\" else sprintf(\"  val acc %.4f\", val_acc)))\n",
        "  }\n",
        "  list(model = model, hist = hist)\n",
        "}"
      ]
    },
