      "source": [
        "## 15. Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | What it adds | Typical accuracy |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Hand-built 2-layer network (Part A) | backprop, Adam and dropout, written from scratch | ~98% |\n",
        "| Single CNN with augmentation (Part B) | convolutions, batch norm, augmentation | ~99.4–99.6% |\n",
        "| Ensemble of CNNs on all data (submission) | averaging several models | ~99.5–99.7% |\n",
        "\n",
        "**What we learned**\n",
        "\n",
        "- A neural network is just matrix multiplications, a non-linearity, a loss, and the chain rule. Part A builds every piece by hand.\n",
        "- For images, **architecture matters**: a CNN's built-in understanding of local 2D patterns beats a much larger fully connected network.\n",
        "- **Augmentation, regularisation and ensembling** each give reliable gains on top of a good architecture.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Ideas to try next**\n",
        "\n",
        "- Train more models in the ensemble, or for more epochs\n",
        "- Tune the augmentation strength (`max_rot`, `max_zoom`, `max_shift`)\n",
        "- Test-time augmentation: average predictions over a few slightly shifted copies of each test image\n",
        "- Wider or deeper CNN blocks (for example 64 → 128 filters)"
      ]
